Handle GPIO0..3 wake IRQ during Free PiZZa suspend

Symptom on first-light: after enter_suspend_mode() reaches
"SDRAM in self-refresh, PLL powered down" and the VPU is in
sleep-waiting-for-GPIO17, pressing the wake button produces

    VPU Received interrupt from source 113   <- GPIO_INT0 slot
    (our v1 handler here)
    VPU Received interrupt from source 116   <- GPIO_INT3 slot
    panic(): "unknown interrupt source!"@trap.c:147

Sources 113..116 map to INTERRUPT_HW_OFFSET (64) + 49..52 =
INTERRUPT_GPIO0..GPIO3, the four VC4 IC0 slots fed by BCM2835's
GPIO interrupt mux. Empirically, a single GPIO bank-0 event
(GPIO17 falling edge) asserts BOTH GPIO_INT0 (49) and GPIO_INT3
(52) simultaneously -- src1 = 0x00120000 in the trap dump has
bits 17 and 20 set. The mux drives GPIO_INT0 as "bank 0" and
GPIO_INT3 as a catch-all for all pins.

Also relevant: interrupt.c's setup_irq_handlers enables ALL 64
external IRQs on core 0 by default. So configure_gpio3_wake's
explicit enable of slot 49 is redundant, and slots 50/51/52 are
also pre-enabled and will fire when the mux drives them.

Upstream sleh_irq only handles TIMER0 and ARM; every other source
falls to the default panic.

Fix by adding a joint case for INTERRUPT_GPIO0..GPIO3 that:

 - Leaves GPEDS0 alone (wait_for_gpio3_wake in src/suspend.c does
   the GPEDS0 ack after breaking out of its poll loop).
 - Disables ALL FOUR IC0 slots (49-52) in one write. All four
   slots live in the same 32-bit word at IC0_BASE + 0x28:
     slot 49 = bits [7:4],  slot 50 = [11:8],
     slot 51 = [15:12],     slot 52 = [19:16]
   So mask = 0x000FFFF0.
   Without this, the source stays asserted after we return and
   we storm back into the vector before the poll loop can
   re-check GPEDS0.

The IC0_BASE + 0x28 slot arithmetic mirrors what
configure_gpio3_wake() in src/suspend.c already computes for
intno 49; kept inline here to avoid pulling interrupt.h into
trap.c or exporting suspend-owned constants upstream.

Apply with `git apply --ignore-whitespace` (trap.c has CRLF
endings, patch generated as LF).

Applied against pristine librerpi/rpi-open-firmware submodule
2725d94.

diff --git a/firmware/trap.c b/firmware/trap.c
index 738fefa..a65d8a8 100644
--- a/firmware/trap.c
+++ b/firmware/trap.c
@@ -137,6 +137,14 @@ void sleh_irq(vc4_saved_state_t* pcb, uint32_t tp) {
   case INTERRUPT_ARM:
     arm_monitor_interrupt();
     break;
+  case INTERRUPT_GPIO0:
+  case INTERRUPT_GPIO1:
+  case INTERRUPT_GPIO2:
+  case INTERRUPT_GPIO3: {
+    volatile uint32_t *ic_slot = (volatile uint32_t *)(0x7E002000 + 0x28);
+    *ic_slot &= ~0x000FFFF0u;
+    return;
+  }
   default:
     print_vpu_state(pcb);
     panic("unknown interrupt source!");
